message.content:
{
  "technical_and_design_decisions": [
    "All new public API functions will adhere to existing naming conventions and structural patterns of the fabric-config library to maintain consistency for existing consumers.",
    "The bulk CLI tool will leverage existing fabric-config library core functions for all config manipulation logic to avoid code duplication and ensure alignment with library behavior.",
    "All new functions will preserve unmodified configuration fields by default, matching the existing Get/Set configuration pattern of the library.",
    "The RemoveLegacyOrdererAddresses and RemoveKafkaBrokers functions will return explicit errors if called on configurations that do not contain the respective legacy fields to prevent accidental removal of valid configuration values.",
    "Consenter removal functions will require an exact match of all 4 identifier fields (host, port, client TLS certificate, server TLS certificate) to ensure safe removal and avoid accidental deletion of incorrect consenter entries.",
    "The bulk CLI tool will use the official Fabric SDK for connection profile parsing, peer discovery, and transaction submission to ensure compatibility with existing Fabric network deployments.",
    "All new API functions will include upfront input validation to provide clear, actionable error messages to consumers."
  ],
  "assumptions": [
    "The existing fabric-config library codebase is fully accessible, well-documented, and has no architectural blockers that would prevent the addition of the specified new functions.",
    "The development environment is preconfigured with all required dependencies, including the Go toolchain, Fabric SDK, and existing test infrastructure for the fabric-config library.",
    "Existing unit and integration test patterns for the fabric-config library can be reused for new test cases, with no need to build new test infrastructure from scratch.",
    "The connection profile format specified in user story U6 is fully compatible with the parsing logic of the official Fabric SDK.",
    "All required changes are confined to the fabric-config library and the new bulk CLI tool; no modifications to core Hyperledger Fabric components are needed.",
    "Existing code examples in the fabric-config repository can be extended to demonstrate new functionality without requiring full rewrites.",
    "The Fabric crypto libraries available in the development environment support all required certificate validation and signing operations for the CLI tool."
  ],
  "activities": [
    {
      "activity_id": "A1",
      "activity_name": "Implement Add Consortium API (U1)",
      "activity_description": "Design and implement the public API function to add a new consortium to the consortiums group, add input validation for edge cases (e.g., empty consortium name, no orgs added post-creation with appropriate error/warning handling), update existing code examples to demonstrate adding a new consortium followed by adding orgs to the consortium.",
      "most_likely_effort": 3
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A2",
      "activity_name": "Implement Signing Identity Optional Config Update Envelope (U2)",
      "activity_description": "Implement the public API function that returns a cb.ConfigUpdateEnvelope without requiring signing identities to be provided at generation time, add input validation for config update inputs, update relevant examples to demonstrate the new optional signing identity flow.",
      "most_likely_effort": 2
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A3",
      "activity_name": "Implement Legacy Orderer Address Removal and Genesis Block Update (U3)",
      "activity_description": "Implement the RemoveLegacyOrdererAddresses function for the top-level channel group, add validation to block direct updates to the OrdererAddresses field (only allow removal via the new function), update genesis block generation logic to omit the top-level OrdererAddresses field and require orderer orgs to specify orderer endpoints, update examples to demonstrate the removal function and new genesis block creation flow.",
      "most_likely_effort": 3
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A4",
      "activity_name": "Implement KafkaBrokers Removal and Migration Example (U4)",
      "activity_description": "Implement the public API function to entirely remove the KafkaBrokers section from orderer configuration, add validation to ensure the function is intended for migrated config cleanup, add/improve examples demonstrating Kafka to EtcdRaft migration including the new removal function.",
      "most_likely_effort": 2
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A5",
      "activity_name": "Implement EtcdRaft Consenter Add/Remove Functions (U5)",
      "activity_description": "Implement public API functions to add and remove consenters from the etcdraft orderer configuration, add validation for removal to require exact match of all 4 fields (host, port, client TLS cert, server TLS cert) to ensure safe removal, update examples to demonstrate the new consenter management functions.",
      "most_likely_effort": 3
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A6",
      "activity_name": "Implement Bulk CLI Tool Core Logic (U6)",
      "activity_description": "Implement the core CLI tool structure, implement JSON parsing for batchUpdate.json, connectionProfile.json, and signingIdentities.json input files, implement dry-run mode that outputs the calculated config update to stdout without submission, implement input validation to return errors for unsupported operations, implement logic to stack multiple operations in a single batch.",
      "most_likely_effort": 5
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A7",
      "activity_name": "Implement Bulk CLI Channel Operations and Fabric Interaction (U6)",
      "activity_description": "Implement all supported bulk operations: channel MSP update (single signature required), TLS cert update for orderer consenter set, V1 to V2 migration (remove dead consenter, remove dead anchor peers, add anchor peers), implement connection profile parsing for peer discovery and config block fetching, implement config update submission to the orderer using provided signing identities.",
      "most_likely_effort": 6
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A8",
      "activity_name": "Implement Individual Orderer Config Update Functions (U7)",
      "activity_description": "Implement all required individual orderer configuration update functions: SetMaxMessageCount, SetAbsoluteMaxBytes, SetPreferredMaxBytes, SetBatchTimeout, SetMaxChannels, SetConsensusType, SetConsensusState, add functions for modifying individual EtcdRaftMetadata values/options, ensure all functions persist existing values for unmodified fields, update examples to demonstrate both the new individual update functions and the existing Get/SetConfiguration flow.",
      "most_likely_effort": 6
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A9",
      "activity_name": "Implement Individual MSP Update Functions (U8)",
      "activity_description": "Implement all required individual MSP configuration update functions for OrdererOrgGroup, ApplicationOrgGroup, and ConsortiumOrgGroup: AddRootCert, RemoveRootCert, AddIntermediateCert, RemoveIntermediateCert, AddAdminCert, RemoveAdminCert, AddCRL, RemoveCRL, AddOUIdentifier, RemoveOUIdentifier, SetCryptoConfig, AddTLSRootCert, RemoveTLSRootCert, AddTLSIntermediateCert, RemoveTLSIntermediateCert, SetClientOUIdentifier, SetPeerOUIdentifier, SetAdminOUIdentifier, SetOrdererOUIdentifier, EnableNodeOUs, DisableNodeOUs, add required certificate validation logic, update examples to demonstrate both the new individual update functions and the existing Get/SetMSP flow for all org group types.",
      "most_likely_effort": 8
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A10",
      "activity_name": "Unit and Integration Testing",
      "activity_description": "Write unit tests for all new API functions and CLI tool components covering edge cases and error conditions, write integration tests for end-to-end flows (e.g., consortium addition, orderer address removal, bulk CLI operations against a test Fabric network), fix any bugs identified during testing.",
      "most_likely_effort": 5
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A11",
      "activity_name": "Documentation and Example Finalization",
      "activity_description": "Update the fabric-config library README and API documentation to include all new functions and usage guidelines, verify all code examples are correct and runnable, add documentation for the new bulk CLI tool including usage instructions, input format specifications, and the example command specified in user story U6.",
      "most_likely_effort": 2
    }
  ],
  "reported_total": {
    "most_likely_effort": 45
  }
}

